# Prerequisites
*.d

# Object files
*.o
*.ko
*.obj
*.elf

# Linker output
*.ilk
*.map
*.exp

# Precompiled Headers
*.gch
*.pch

# Libraries
# NB: *.a is deliberately NOT ignored here - ACME uses .a for 6502 source files
# (see its docs: "Please use '.a' as the file name extension of ACME source
# code files"), so ignoring it would silently drop assembly sources.
*.lib
*.la
*.lo

# Shared objects (inc. Windows DLLs)
*.dll
*.so
*.so.*
*.dylib

# Executables
*.exe
*.out
*.app
*.i*86
*.x86_64
*.hex

# Debug files
*.dSYM/
*.su
*.idb
*.pdb

# Kernel Module Compile Results
*.mod*
*.cmd
.tmp_versions/
modules.order
Module.symvers
Mkfile.old
dkms.conf

# debug information files
*.dwo

# Claude Code state staged for the first devcontainer rebuild (contains credentials)
.devcontainer/.claude-seed/

# Claude Code: track this project's own instructions, skills and non-skill MCP
# server implementations, ignore the installed toolkit (agents, commands, hooks,
# gsd-core and local settings are per-machine)
#
# CLAUDE.md is tracked as of 2026-08-01. It was never per-machine -- it carries
# the project's own standing rules, including the hard rule that mcp__vice__*
# is the only route to the emulator. Being caught by the blanket `.claude/*`
# meant those rules lived in one working copy and a fresh clone silently got
# none of them, which is the wrong failure direction for a rule whose whole job
# is to stop something being rebuilt.
.claude/*
!.claude/CLAUDE.md
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/mcp/

# scratch notes
anything.*

# transient VICE probe screenshots (evidence is re-captured by tools/recover.mjs)
recovery/*/dumps/probe-*.png

# host-side VICE supervisor output (tools/vice-supervisor.sh): crash logs and
# the restart epoch file, regenerated fresh on every supervisor start -- not
# a project artifact, just evidence for the current debugging session.
# The .bak-* form is the same state moved aside during a clean-slate restart
# (see 01.2-CRITERION-13-EVIDENCE.md § 1) -- kept on disk for its crash logs,
# still not a project artifact.
.vice-supervisor/
.vice-supervisor.bak-*/

# deployed copies of .claude/mcp/vice/resources/ -- the tracked source of
# truth lives in that directory (the vice MCP implementation, not a skill);
# these are regenerated automatically by install-resources.mjs the first time
# any .claude/mcp/vice/ .mjs entry point runs, and are disposable: never
# hand-edit them here (edit resources/ instead), and a real host setup keeps
# working exactly as before because they still land at these same paths.
# vice-broker.sh (Phase 01.2) joins the supervisor and pool scripts here.
/tools/vice-supervisor.sh
/tools/vice-pool.sh
/tools/vice-broker.sh
/tools/lib/container-guard.sh
/tools/lib/repo-root.sh
